+# Metadata for this hypothesis. Keep it current; the report prints it.
+question = "Given the posterior at 00:11 and fuel exhaustion, where, when and how energetically did the aircraft reach the sea, under each explicitly weighted end-of-flight family (controlled glide, ditching, unpiloted spiral/phugoid, dive), with and without the 00:19 transmissions?"
+# open | supported | not-supported | inconclusive
+status = "open"
+# One line, written when the question is answered, citing the run that answered it.
+summary = ""
+# Changes needed in the core (new hooks, new state fields). Leave empty if none.
+# A hypothesis agent writes requests here and stops; it never edits core code.
+core_requests = [
+    "Terminal hook, two calls per trajectory: takeover_time(handoff at 00:11, fuel, uniforms) -> (unix_s of the FIRST flame-out, log proposal correction); the runner flies the core dynamics to that time; then descend(state at takeover, atmosphere, uniforms, requested epochs) -> descent samples with impact fields, the state (lat, lon, alt, velocity east/north/up) at each requested 00:19 epoch, and a log proposal correction.",
+    "Atmosphere access inside the terminal hook: wind and temperature at (unix_s, alt_ft, lat, lon), a trait in crates/hypothesis implemented by the runner over the ERA5 grid (500-43,000 ft, 17:00-01:00).",
+    "Exact 00:19 epochs: R600 00:19:29.416 and R1200 00:19:37.443 (data/satcom-observations.csv rounds both to whole seconds); BFOs 182 and -2 Hz; the start-up BFO offset (Holland 2018) is a core measurement-model option.",
+    "Scoring callback: log-likelihood of the config-selected 00:19 observations for a candidate descent's epoch states, used only to adapt the defensive-mixture proposal; final weights stay exact (module returns log p/q, runner scores each observation once).",
+    "Runner-supplied uniforms as a stream (FnMut() -> f64, seeded per descent), because the number of draws varies with family and proposal.",
+    "When fuel lands: per trajectory, the second (left) flame-out time or the fuel state implying it, the mass, and ideally the left/right fuel imbalance.",
+    "Terminal hook docs: takeover_time is 'when the module takes over' (a flame-out, or the start of a powered descent), possibly after 00:19:37; a takeover after the last epoch leaves the epoch list empty.",
+]
